# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: The Crooked Tree collapses into a bed of glowing coals, and up in the night sky, the bound queen twists behind the silver bars of the moon.
Narrator: Lord Phillip and Lady Adela hold fast to one another in the clearing, their tired shapes dissolving into warm golden dust on the wind.
Narrator: Beside Adela's fading light, the embers of the fallen climb through the blackened branches to keep their watch above the valley.
Narrator: When the Ghostlight Express hisses to a halt at the moorland station, you step aboard with the smell of woodsmoke still clinging to your coats.
Narrator: The plush velvet seats across the aisle remain empty, holding only the quiet weight of those who stayed behind at the skull.
if flag.last_act_count >= 2
Narrator: More than one place stands open in the warm yellow lamplight, a row of silent cushions where old friends ought to sit.
endif
Narrator: The Vagrant walks the narrow aisle and lays a punched brass ticket on each cushion, one for every soul who boarded and one for every soul who did not.
the_vagrant [weary]: They bought your passage with their own bright spark, friends, so keep their names warm wherever the rails take you.
Narrator: The iron wheels catch the track, and the train carries you softly out of Druskenvald through the parting mist.
-> END
